  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Cumene is an organic compound obtained by&nbsp;Friedel-Crafts alkylation of benzene with&nbsp;propylene. Upon oxidation of cumene (isopropylbenzene) in the presence of air, cumene hydroperoxide is obtained. Upon further treatment of cumene hydroperoxide with dilute acid, phenols are obtained</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0133_0f1259612b63.png\" style=\"width: 576px; height: 223px;\" /><br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0133_ee3b132b23c9.png\" style=\"width: 378px; height: 262px;\" /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0133_b72267f07410.png\" style=\"width: 643px; height: 229px;\" /></p>"
